# --------------------- gwf vset options ---------------------
# flopy multi-package
# package-type stress-package

block options
name et_model
type string
valid feddes
reader urword
optional true
longname model used for the root-water uptake reduction
description is a text keyword to indicate which model is used to reduce potential transpiration to actual root-water uptake as a function of pressure head.  Currently only FEDDES is supported, which is also the default.

block options
name h1
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname feddes anoxia pressure head
description is the pressure head ($L$) at and above which root-water uptake is zero because of oxygen stress (the anoxia point) in the Feddes model.  Pressure heads must satisfy H1 $>$ H2 $>$ H3 $>$ H4.

block options
name h2
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname feddes upper optimal pressure head
description is the pressure head ($L$) below which root-water uptake is at the potential rate (the wet end of the optimal range) in the Feddes model.

block options
name h3
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname feddes lower optimal pressure head
description is the pressure head ($L$) above which root-water uptake is at the potential rate (the dry end of the optimal range) in the Feddes model.

block options
name h4
type double precision
reader urword
optional true
longname feddes wilting point pressure head
description is the pressure head ($L$) at and below which root-water uptake is zero because of water stress (the wilting point) in the Feddes model.

block options
name auxiliary
type string
shape (naux)
reader urword
optional true
longname keyword to specify aux variables
description REPLACE auxnames {'{#1}': 'Groundwater Flow'}

block options
name auxmultname
type string
shape
reader urword
optional true
longname name of auxiliary variable for multiplier
description REPLACE auxmultname {'{#1}': 'transpiration rate'}

block options
name boundnames
type keyword
shape
reader urword
optional true
longname
description REPLACE boundnames {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}

block options
name print_input
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print input to listing file
description REPLACE print_input {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}
mf6internal iprpak

block options
name print_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print transpiration rates to listing file
description REPLACE print_flows {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}
mf6internal iprflow

block options
name save_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname save transpiration rates to budget file
description REPLACE save_flows {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}
mf6internal ipakcb

block options
name ts_filerecord
type record ts6 filein ts6_filename
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name ts6
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname head keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to a time-series file.

block options
name filein
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an input filename is expected next.

block options
name ts6_filename
type string
preserve_case true
in_record true
reader urword
optional false
tagged false
longname file name of time series information
description REPLACE timeseriesfile {}

block options
name obs_filerecord
type record obs6 filein obs6_filename
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name obs6
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname obs keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to an observations file.

block options
name obs6_filename
type string
preserve_case true
in_record true
tagged false
reader urword
optional false
longname obs6 input filename
description REPLACE obs6_filename {'{#1}': 'VSET', '{#2}': '\\ref{table:gwf-obstypetable}'}

# --------------------- gwf vset dimensions ---------------------

block dimensions
name maxbound
type integer
reader urword
optional false
longname maximum number of transpiration cells
description REPLACE maxbound {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}

# --------------------- gwf vset period ---------------------

block period
name iper
type integer
block_variable true
in_record true
tagged false
shape
valid
reader urword
optional false
longname stress period number
description REPLACE iper {}

block period
name stress_period_data
type recarray cellid rate aux boundname
shape (maxbound)
reader urword
longname
description
mf6internal spd

block period
name cellid
type integer
shape (ncelldim)
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
longname cell identifier
description REPLACE cellid {}

block period
name rate
type double precision
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
time_series true
longname potential transpiration rate
description is the potential transpiration flux rate ($LT^{-1}$) for the cell, interpreted as the root-fraction-weighted atmospheric demand assigned to this cell.  Actual root-water uptake is this rate reduced by the pressure-head stress response of the selected ET model.  If the Options block includes a TIMESERIESFILE entry (see the ``Time-Variable Input'' section), values can be obtained from a time series by entering the time-series name in place of a numeric value.

block period
name aux
type double precision
in_record true
tagged false
shape (naux)
reader urword
optional true
time_series true
longname auxiliary variables
description REPLACE aux {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}
mf6internal auxvar

block period
name boundname
type string
shape
tagged false
in_record true
reader urword
optional true
longname transpiration name
description REPLACE boundname {'{#1}': 'transpiration'}
